WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:02.211
♪♪

00:00:02.211 --> 00:00:05.172
Narrator:
Would you describe your child as
strong-willed,...

00:00:05.172 --> 00:00:05.923
♪♪

00:00:05.923 --> 00:00:06.840
Narrator:
...rambunctious,...

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.674
♪♪

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.175
Narrator:
...unkempt?

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:09.009
(Ahh)

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.470
Narrator:
Has their sleep been irregular?

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.847
Narrator:
Do they have mysterious
scratches?

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.099
Narrator:
Have your laundry loads doubled
in size?

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:17.142
Narrator:
Have they gone feral?

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:18.644
(Howling)

00:00:18.644 --> 00:00:20.938
Narrator:
Have you been wondering 
what exactly changed?

00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:23.232
Narrator:
Well there's an answer to your
question.

00:00:23.232 --> 00:00:26.652
Narrator:
Your child just might be...a
"Wolfwalker".

00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:29.404
♪♪

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:31.823
Sean Óg:
She's one of them Wolfwalkers.

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:33.075
Wolfwalkers?

00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:35.744
The one's that can talk to
wolves.

00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:37.996
Narrator:
Raising a Wolfwalker is a
demanding job,

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:39.498
Narrator:
but ultimately rewarding.

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:42.167
You have four legs now, you can
run really fast.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.253
Narrator:
Here are a few tips that may
help you adjust.

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:45.254
(Burping)
(Bird squawking)

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:48.674
Narrator:
First, make sure your child gets
plenty of time in nature.

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:52.094
Stay here in the forest, it's
great.

00:00:52.094 --> 00:00:55.472
Narrator:
And they'll need exercise, lots
of exercise.

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:57.891
Narrator:
And you should probably keep an
eye on them.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.103
Narrator:
Wolfwalkers have a way of
getting into trouble.

00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:02.854
(Chicken clucking)
What?

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:05.023
Stay inside, do as you're told.

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:07.150
Narrator:
A Wolfwalker child can be a
handful.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.778
Narrator:
So remember to reach out when
you need a helping hand.

00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:12.281
Narrator:
Some people don't quite
understand the

00:01:12.281 --> 00:01:13.907
Narrator:
wild nature of a Wolfwalker.
(Barking)

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.367
(Bell ringing)
Wolf, wolf!

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.452
Narrator:
So make sure they're
self-reliant

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:18.328
Narrator:
and resourceful.

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:19.538
(Kids "aww")

00:01:19.538 --> 00:01:21.707
Narrator:
And don't forget about
self care.

00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:25.043
Narrator:
Because you aren't going to get
any sleep with a Wolfwalker on your hands.

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:28.755
(Aww)
-Narrator:
For additional tips watch "Wolfwalkers" on Apple TV+.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.841
♪♪

00:01:30.841 --> 00:01:34.720
(Howling)

